WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:05.690
Jordan Peele's Get Out had a lot to say, but
Us is arguably twice as ambitious, doubling

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:08.080
down on both the horror and the social commentary.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.330
But if you didn't quite catch what the movie
was going for, then it might also be a frustrating

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:12.820
watch.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.780
There's a lot going on beneath the surface
of this movie - and we mean that literally.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.820
The premise of Us revolves around sinister,
slasher-movie doppelgangers, who show up out

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.160
of nowhere with apparently murderous motives.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.320
It supposedly focuses on one family, the Wilsons,
being attacked in a home invasion by brutal

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.600
copies of themselves.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.500
But the third act reveals that it's not just
the Wilsons having this strange experience

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.410
- it's the entire United States of America,
with an unfathomably huge army of doubles

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:44.060
being led by a woman named Red, the shadow
version of Lupita Nyong'o's Adelaide.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.699
That's the first twist the movie throws at
you.

00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:50.780
But the second big twist, teased out slowly,
is that the Addie the audience has been following

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:55.170
the whole movie isn't the original Adelaide
- it's her double, who switched places with

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:58.080
her at a young age during the movie's opening
flashback scene.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:02.879
Grown-up Addie is haunted by an experience
from her youth, when she wandered into a boardwalk

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.440
funhouse and saw a sinister vision of herself.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:09.940
But the movie leaves out crucial information
of what happened during that encounter, apparently

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:12.970
reflecting the fact that Addie herself has
suppressed what happened.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.920
As she recalls, she wandered into the attraction,
found herself, and then shortly returned to

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.080
her panicking parents.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:23.240
But as the final frames of the movie reveal,
a whole lot of consequential stuff happened

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.280
during that brief period - like the fact that
the original Addie never came back.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:31.880
In the movie's final moments, Addie realizes
- or perhaps just finally admits to herself

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:36.170
- that she is the double from the underground,
who strangled the original Addie and took

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:40.200
her place, leaving the original Addie shackled
down below to begin a new life as Red.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.700
One big clue that this is what happened is
that Red is the only one of the doubles that

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.200
can talk.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:48.820
Everyone else only emits inhuman grunts and
moans, with Red speaking in a raspy, damaged

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:49.320
voice.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.680
Turns out, this comes from the damage her
double did to her throat when she strangled

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:53.180
her.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:57.000
When the double entered the real world, she
still didn't know how to speak, leaving her

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.640
parents baffled at their daughter's sudden,
apparently trauma-induced muteness.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:05.640
Addie spends the first act sporting a serious
sense of dread, but the twist changes our

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.550
perception of what that dread is all about.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:11.900
While it's played somewhat ambiguously, it
seems like the adult Addie truly does not

00:02:11.909 --> 00:02:14.530
know, at the beginning of the movie, where
she really came from.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:17.580
But she knows something is wrong, and that
a reckoning is coming.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:18.360
"I think…

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:22.500
I feel like it means she's getting closer."

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:27.549
The first thing most people did when they
got home from seeing Us was probably Google

00:02:27.549 --> 00:02:31.650
the phrase "Jeremiah 11:11," which turns up
in the film multiple times.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:36.109
Though translations differ, the sentiment
of that Bible passage is pretty clear: "It's

00:02:36.109 --> 00:02:36.760
payback time."

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:40.200
The International Standard Version of the
passage translates into:

00:02:40.209 --> 00:02:43.630
"I'm about to bring disaster on them from
which they won't be able to escape.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.780
They'll cry out to me, but I won't listen
to them."

00:02:46.109 --> 00:02:50.239
It's clear what's being set up here — an
us vs. them conflict between the oppressed

00:02:50.239 --> 00:02:55.000
tethered underclass and the ignorant, privileged
surface dwellers, led by Red — the original

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:55.500
Adelaide.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:59.860
One big thing the Red twist does is completely
recontextualize who the viewer should be rooting

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.000
for in the story.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:05.960
Red still became a bad person, but realizing
why she's so thirsty for revenge against Addie

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:08.520
makes her a sympathetic villain — and vice
versa.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:13.640
One person who clearly picks up on Addie's
otherworldly nature is her son Jason, who

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:17.360
witnesses her growling and snarling her way
through several fights in the movie.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.719
While he doesn't say anything about it, he
comes to increasingly regard his mother with

00:03:21.719 --> 00:03:26.029
apprehension, even terror, realizing that
the woman he thought he knew may not be who

00:03:26.029 --> 00:03:26.920
she's said she is.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:31.420
At the end of the movie, as Addie realizes
her true nature while Jason watches, Jason

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:35.439
pulls his mask down on his head — to which
Addy smiles in response, putting on a mask

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.000
of her own.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:40.960
Addie's true nature as a tethered person also
comes into play during some of her more inexplicable

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:45.409
actions, like getting out of the car to watch
the Zora double die, or refusing to strike

00:03:45.409 --> 00:03:48.380
the double of Jason when he confronts them
near a burning car.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:52.560
Her actions don't seem to make sense, until
you understand what she's realizing: These

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.360
people are her people, and maybe she doesn't
want to hurt them after all.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:00.900
The question of who created the tethered doesn't
get answered — and that's probably for the

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:01.400
best.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.739
It's also what Jordan Peele intended, with
many of the movie's specifics being intentionally

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:07.120
open to interpretation.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.860
Think of it less like a puzzle, and more like
an ink blot.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:14.660
"I want to leave some runway for people to
explore what it means to them."

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:17.880
While the viewer might first think that Addie's
visit to the mirror maze is what triggered

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:22.400
the creation of her double, the ending demonstrates
that the doubles already existed underground

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.560
long before she arrived.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:24.260
How?

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:27.740
It's unknown, it's designed to be that way,
and it's really not important.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:31.160
No answer on this Earth would be as satisfying
as the mystery feels.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:35.470
The most obvious explanation is that the doubles
come from a secret government experiment — an

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:40.320
unfathomably massive cloning project of some
sort that copied every American's body while

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.960
failing to replicate the soul.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:46.220
But since the scale of such an operation seems
impossible for humans to accomplish, it's

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.470
hard to take this explanation at face value.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:53.140
In a logistical sense, nothing can explain
how the doubles are created — much less

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:57.620
how they got 300 million pairs of scissors,
Freddy Krueger gloves, and red jumpsuits.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:01.610
The fact is, the real villains of the movie
are the people who set up this deranged experiment

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.140
before abandoning its subjects.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.940
But whoever these people are, they never actually
appear.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:10.430
Without the ability to identify, confront,
and fight back against their real oppressors,

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:12.440
the characters instead tear each other apart.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:16.380
And that sounds like a big fat metaphor for
American society to us.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:17.720
"We are our own worst enemy."

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:22.880
Jordan Peele has described Us as being about
the fear of the other, and the self-destructive

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.830
tendencies that fear can cultivate.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:28.460
With this framework in mind, the tethered
can represent a lot of different groups.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:32.900
Maybe it's all the people that American society
has condemned over the centuries — victims

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:37.160
of the slave trade, mass incarceration, racism,
or a predatory class divide.

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:40.880
They represent the forgotten Americans who
fall through the wide holes in the country's

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.200
social safety nets — the people we abandon.

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:47.440
The striking final shots of the movie show
these people stretched across the continent

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:50.940
in a human chain, hand-in-hand beneath the
blue sky and the sun.

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:54.660
For so long, they suffered, living only a
shadow of the good life that their doubles

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:55.160
enjoyed.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.280
Not anymore, though.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:06:00.200
It took a lot of killing to get topside, but
considering the suffering they went through,

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.390
it's almost hard to blame them for making
the effort.

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:05.440
Remember what Red told Adelaide — they're
humans, too, you know.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:06.480
Just like us.

